  "reading": "Consistent with generation-2 pauses, and not established as caused by them market by market. For it: the run's 215 full collections cost 134.0 s, a mean of 623 ms each, which is the magnitude of the large maxima; and in the twenty worst markets the decide, prepare and reconcile stage maxima are 1-20 ms, two orders of magnitude below the observe maximum, so the time is spent around the cycle rather than inside the strategy or the reconciler. Against it: full collections occur in 82 % of quiet markets too, so their presence alone separates nothing. Exact per-market attribution is not possible from this run because GcObserver records a run-cumulative maximum rather than a per-market one \u2014 an instrumentation gap, and one of the things a runtime-engineering phase should fix first.",
